usage: migrate_sqlite_to_postgres.py [-h] [--dsn DSN] [--verify-only]
                                     sqlite_path

Copy a stopped, verified Tempo SQLite snapshot into PostgreSQL. The
destination must have all checked-in migrations applied and no application
rows. Each table is copied in a separate transaction and recorded in
tempo_migration_progress, so an interrupted import can resume safely. Run
--verify-only afterward to compare every row in primary-key order.

positional arguments:
  sqlite_path

options:
  -h, --help     show this help message and exit
  --dsn DSN
  --verify-only
